# Biome over the staged files only. This is the same `biome check` that `ci-cli`
# runs as a required check, narrowed to what you are about to commit, so it
# finishes in well under a second on a normal change.
#
# It checks, it does not write. A hook that rewrote your files would have to
# re-stage them, and on a partially staged file that means committing hunks you
# never staged. When this fails, run `bun run format`, read the diff, stage it.
#
# `git commit --no-verify` skips this. `ci-cli` does not skip.
bun run lint:staged
